      "title": "Project Asst. - Lichen and Bryophyte Technician - R. Thiet [Work Study]",
      "description": "Project Asst. - Lichen and Bryophyte Technician - R. Thiet [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Coalition for the Common Good Equity, Belonging, and Culture History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Project Asst. - Lichen and Bryophyte Technician - R. Thiet [Work Study] Project Asst. - Lichen and Bryophyte Technician - R. Thiet [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 4 days ago Antioch University New England * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 9/1/2026 End Date: 12/12/2026 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 2 0 hrs / week Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Rachel Thiet Alternate Supervisor: Meaghan Guckian, ES PhD Program Director This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 70% of work will be remote and will involve analyzing field and laboratory samples, data management, and data analysis. Method to assess remote work: I plan to meet regularly with the technician to discuss workflow and oversee work quality. Job Description The Lichen and Bryophyte Technician will identify bryophytes and lichens in field samples (1 hr / week); analyze soil samples containing lichens and bryophytes (3 hrs / week); manage a complex data set (3 hrs / week); and perform complex data analysis (3 hrs / week). Qualifications 1. Familiarity with lichen and bryophyte ID and ecology. 2. Strong data management and analysis skills. 3. Strong attention to detail. 4. Willingness and ability and learn complex new skills largely independently. 5. Strong communication skills. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Submit an updated CV and letter of interest. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Environmental Studies To apply for this job email your details to rthiet@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Announcing the New President of Antioch University Learn More"
