    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/program-coordinator-cto-part-time/": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, CTO (part time)",
      "description": "Program Coordinator, CTO (part time) - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Coalition for the Common Good Equity, Belonging, and Culture History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Program Coordinator, CTO (part time) Program Coordinator, CTO (part time) Staff Los Angeles, CA Posted 5 days ago Antioch University Los Angeles Program: Masters in Clinical Psychology (MAP) Classification: Staff, Part-time, Non-Exempt (No Benefits) Reports to: Director of Clinical Training Office Location: Antioch University Los Angeles, Los Angeles, CA Campus Compensation: Antioch University offers a competitive compensation and benefits package that includes both direct and indirect pay. The compensation will be based on experience, education, knowledge, credentials, and a consideration of the difficulty and complexity of the position. The hourly rate for this position is:  $24.50. Position Summary The Program Coordinator for the Clinical Training Office (CTO), serves as the primary liaison between students, faculty in the Masters of Clinical Psychology (MAP), the CTO Director, and other offices. The Program Coordinator administers the operations of the Antioch University Los Angeles Clinical Training Office, supporting Masters in Psychology students, Clinical Training sites and Clinical Faculty and collaborating with other Antioch University Clinical Training Offices and University departments such as Student Services and Registrar Office. Essential Duties and Responsibilities CTO Administration Support student learning through distribution and collection of a range of evaluation instruments and processes relevant to practicum classes and clinical site placements. Provide clear, accessible instruction and guidance to students preparing for and engaged in clinical training. Responsibilities may include developing video, PowerPoint, and zoom presentations to inform students of policies and guidelines required of trainees, as well as introductions to the required Tevera documentation platform. Provide administrative support to Clinical Faculty including support of internal and external communications with students and clinical sites, scheduling, data collection, etc. Coordinate and support CTO-focused events in support of student learning outcomes and stronger internal and external relationships. Events involve a range of professional development opportunities, introductions to sites and their representatives, panel discussions with alumni, etc. Participate fully in CTO-relevant meetings, provide coordination support as needed. Collaborate and coordinate with all CTO staff and faculty to ensure high-quality student clinical training experience and learning outcomes. Program Data Management Maintain all documentation for the CTO office including student records. Manage data integrity and entry with Tavera platform; build CTO-relevant data fields and support students in managing their use of the platform as Prepare and distribute information packets to students and support their efforts to gain their Bureau Behavioral Sciences Associate Collaborate with CTO staff, clinical sites, and other key stakeholders to maintain all CTO databases, contact lists, and archives required by BBS and other institutional Maintain updated mail and e-mail lists of students and site supervisors, directors, and other personnel. Create and maintain reports including compiling statistics for assessment and other purposes. Performs other duties as assigned Antioch University reserves the right to change the duties of the job description at any time. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience, or equivalent education, experience and training; Master’s degree preferred Strong organizational and time management skills Excellent interpersonal, verbal and written communication and customer service skills Proficiency in MS Office and Google Suites, and ability to learn and utilize new software Experience with documents management systems such as Tevera helpful Knowledge of Bureau Behavioral Sciences standards desirable Associate Marriage and Family Therapist (AMFT) and/or equivalent desirable Supervision Received Minimal supervision received Supervision Exercised No supervisory responsibilities Hours of Employment This is a part-time position serving a national university.  A work schedule will be established in consultation with the supervisor. Physical Requirements The essential functions represent the basic job duties that an employee must be able to perform, with or without a reasonable accommodation. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Application Instructions Please email a cover letter, resume, and a list of reference names and contact information to [email protected] . In the subject line of the email, please state Program Coordinator, CTO. Please attach all documents including the cover letter to the email. Coalition for the Common Good (CCG) EEO Statement The Coalition for the Common Good, doing business as Antioch University, provides equal employment opportunity to all employees and applicants and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic or class protected by federal, state or local laws in matters affecting employment or in providing access to programs.  This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruitment, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, benefits, and training. The CCG complies with all state and federal laws that prohibit discrimination, including Title VII of the Civil Rights Act, Title IX, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, the Equal Pay Act and the Age Discrimination in Employment Act. Inquiries should be addressed to the Office of Human Resources or the Office of the General Counsel. Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Announcing the New President of Antioch University Learn More"
    },
