nects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Administrative Assistant - MAP Clinical Training Office - J. Hall [Work Study] Administrative Assistant - MAP Clinical Training Office - J. Hall [Work Study] Work-Study (AULA) Los Angeles Posted 2 months ago Antioch University Los Angeles * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 8/3/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 15 hrs/week - 1 student Weekends Required: Yes Evenings Required: Yes Supervisor: MAP CTO, Jonathan Hall Alternate Supervisor: Jenn Ellingwood This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 80% administrative tasks supporting staff with filing and organizing work as assigned Method to assess remote work: Checking in with student that tasks are completed Job Description Specific responsibilities shall include 1) creating and maintaining electronic files, databases, and cloud-based repositories (5 hours), 2) providing administrative support to program staff, students, and faculty, including drafting and responding to emails (5 hours), and 4) other related duties as assigned (5 hours). Qualifications Candidates should have at least six months left studying at Antioch. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Submit resume to [email protected] Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: MAP Clinical Training Office To apply for this job email your details to jellingwood@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Announcing the New President of Antioch University Learn More"
